From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 03:55:25 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] manager: sound the alert tone, at full volume for
 presidential alerts

Notifications alone make no sound on every desktop: an alert on a muted
phone was only a popup. Sound the EAS attention signal (853 Hz and 960 Hz
together, which Korea's alerts use too) through the PulseAudio API, as
the alert's channel asks:

- alert-sound-full-channels (default 4370, 4383, presidential): on the
  speakers at full volume, unmuted, and on every connected device
  (Bluetooth, USB, headphones) at that device's own volume
- alert-sound-raised-channels (default 4371, 4384): on the connected
  devices only, at their own volume, when there are any; otherwise on the
  speakers at half volume or the user's volume, whichever is higher
- any other channel shown as a notification: a short chime on the
  default output at the user's volume

A connected device keeps its own volume, for the ears it is on. The
speakers' volume and mute are put back when the tone is over, unless the
user changed them meanwhile. With no speaker or connected device known,
the tone goes to the default output rather than nowhere.

Signed-off-by: Noa Himesaka <himesaka@noa.codes>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
